    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n3680" root="بين" body-key="b">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُبِينٌ</span></b>  <i>Separating, severing, disuniting,</i> or <i>cutting off;</i> (S, K;) as also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُبْيِنٌ</span>, like <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُحْسِنٌ</span>:
(K:) but [the right reading in the K may be
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وَمُبِينٌ كَمُحْسِنٍ</span>, meaning "and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُبِينٌ</span> is like
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُحْسِنٌ</span>:" if not,] <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُبْيِنٌ</span> is a mistake. (TA.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2- 
See also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَيِّنٌ</span>, in two places.

